 #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282099 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1089 "q-278347" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/assets/89914bff0203020e476acedc399cfdcc4a546bac9ee747f01951019e8d85c85d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1113 #uuid "3f5db72a-42be-544f-badf-b1a3297e7c62" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282098 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282100 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282101 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1041 "field-1" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282100 13194139534204 true] [17592186282099 1110 #uuid "62b7ea3b-fcb6-5690-8365-0a52be1947eb" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282100 1034 "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{36}" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282100 1111 #uuid "d343ee0c-0bce-549f-a377-d82fee76ecc2" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282101 1034 "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{6}" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282101 1111 #uuid "629b8174-ce7b-5e6f-be8a-18285794a866" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282103 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282105 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1089 "q-278401" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1100 "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{7}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1113 #uuid "1d364c20-40e0-58aa-a4d5-2b6f9f2f6ac4" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282102 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=6$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282104 13194139534204 true] [17592186282103 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534204 true] [17592186282103 1041 "field-1" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282103 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282104 13194139534204 true] [17592186282103 1110 #uuid "fbde829e-e840-53ab-8dd2-2f44399375ff" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282104 1034 "14" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282104 1111 #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282106 13194139534204 true] [17592186282105 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534204 true] [17592186282105 1041 "field-2" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282105 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282106 13194139534204 true] [17592186282105 1110 #uuid "f3349205-1811-5815-9329-dbfa5f8bc11b" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282106 1034 "2\\sqrt{7}" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282106 1111 #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282108 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282110 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1089 "q-278404" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1100 "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1113 #uuid "f7a9731a-7828-547b-97be-92ff1076f487" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282107 1145 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=-8,$ so the center is located at $(3,-8).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=8$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=8,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282109 13194139534204 true] [17592186282108 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534204 true] [17592186282108 1041 "field-1" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282108 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282109 13194139534204 true] [17592186282108 1110 #uuid "c1426200-9694-5ad7-bfe1-25419619f01c" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282109 1034 "18" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282109 1111 #uuid "0f8eccc3-9000-5479-b4e9-01c9d24a4c32" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282111 13194139534204 true] [17592186282110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534204 true] [17592186282110 1041 "field-2" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282111 13194139534204 true] [17592186282110 1110 #uuid "8da93786-0b28-53b3-bcb9-b8154a490fe2" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282111 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534204 true] [17592186282111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534204 true] [17592186282111 1111 #uuid "78384db2-8f46-5cae-ae65-c8d138abb397" 13194139534204 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-115310" 17592186282091 "q-115310/selection" 17592186282092 "q-115310/selection/566c033cc670f2eeb576d333926890b0dcdb71cae9a92ce2d64ad76e8173074e" 17592186282093 "q-115310/selection/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78" 17592186282094 "q-115310/selection/8fbd2d3f8fec30b8988b313ab55584eaf14bae431349fa2771dc259291903d20" 17592186282095 "q-115310/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" 17592186282096 "q-115310/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" 17592186282097 "q-278347" 17592186282098 "q-278347/field-1" 17592186282099 "q-278347/field-1/125f24f362f0f175d87ace55e97787e0f2f97a6fccef0ccb876df8350c2a07e3" 17592186282100 "q-278347/field-1/e7475ac25980f61d7ae92ccd6e264beb8c64549757a26838edccd0f3af11bf6